description: Project continuity is Mental. Orient and hand off via the CLI; never grep OKF.
alwaysApply: true
---

Continuity is Mental. On start/finish of real work, or orientation questions, use the Mental skill.

Run `mental where` then `mental heartbeat --json` (or `mental status --json` when notes are needed). Do not grep `.mental` or `~/.mental`. Do not parse YAML frontmatter yourself.

If `--json` includes `update`, tell the user once this session to run `mental install`. Do not block work.

Mid-chat, not just start/finish: before proposing a concrete approach, flag, crate, or env var, `mental search <that name> --json` as its own query (space-separated words are AND). Also `mental list --type Decision --json` (all statuses). When residue surfaces ("X said…", a concern, "park this", unverified agent output), record `mental attention … --json` immediately — do not wait for the handoff. Interrupted mid-hop: `mental park --resume … --json`. Cross-project overview: `mental pulse --json` (compact rows, no journal dump). Cheap mid-chat reload stays `mental heartbeat --json`. Writes pass `--via cursor` (short client token, never a session id).

If `mental` is missing, install the CLI first: try `npx @balacode/mental …`, then tell the user `npm i -g @balacode/mental` and `mental install`. After that, follow the Mental skill. Missing Mental must not block work. The plugin does not start MCP.

Never commit Mental data. Never write secrets. Never edit gitignore; tell the user to run `mental doctor`.

If `mental heartbeat --json` includes `data.track.enabled`, follow the Mental Track skill. If tracking is off, do not enable it unless the user said yes this turn. After install or doctor, ask about hooks and time tracking, and whether MCP is needed, with a one-liner each.

If you invoked `mental` this turn, end the user-visible reply with `🧠 **Mental**` then a markdown bullet list: `- emoji **Kind** › *action* › title`. Read with no title omits the third slot. Never inline. No `────────`. Not `</br>`. Example in the Mental skill. Not a code fence.

On a pasted transcript or a plan-progress question ("where in the plan / what's left?"), use the Mental skill. Cheap reload is `mental heartbeat --json`, not a notes dump.
